{"content":"\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n\\usepackage[margin=2.4cm]{geometry}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,amsthm,booktabs}\n\\usepackage[capitalize]{cleveref}\n\\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}\n\\newtheorem{lemma}{Lemma}\n\\newtheorem{proposition}{Proposition}\n\\newtheorem{corollary}{Corollary}\n\\newtheorem*{remark}{Remark}\n\\newcommand{\\vt}{v_2}\n\\newcommand{\\Ztwo}{\\mathbb Z_2}\n\\title{Is the Finite-Shadow Language a Faithful Compression\\\\ of Collatz\nDynamics?}\n\\author{John A. Janik\\\\ \\small\\texttt{john.janik@gmail.com}}\n\\date{June 2026}\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nA referee asks: \\emph{how do we know the finite-shadow language\ncaptures all arithmetic mechanisms available to Collatz, rather than\nonly the mechanisms visible to the surviving candidates inside the\nframework?} We answer in four parts. (1) The language is\n\\emph{lossless}, not a projection: the valuation-word coding is a\nhomeomorphic conjugacy of the $2$-adic Syracuse system onto the full\nshift, so no mechanism is discarded at the symbolic level; what the\nlanguage cannot express is exactly one thing --- membership in\n$\\mathbb N\\subset\\Ztwo$ --- and the program imports that through an\nexplicit, enumerable list of archimedean mechanisms (clocks, counting,\nthe drift identity, Baker). (2) Within the finite-modulus category the\nlanguage is provably \\emph{complete}: every observable of a bounded\norbit window modulo any $Q$ coprime to $6$ factors exactly through\n(one residue, the letters), and conditional on any word cylinder the\nresidues at all odd places are exactly equidistributed --- only the\n$2$-adic coordinate feeds the word; every other finite place is a\npassenger. (3) The empirical hidden-channel test is null:\nmultiplicative invariants ($\\omega$, squarefreeness, divisibility,\nprimality) of deep $\\{1,2\\}$-survivors match size-matched controls\nexactly. (4) The ``reversed-flow'' concern conflates presentation with\ncontent: the load-bearing theorems of the program are\n$\\forall$-integer statements in Tao's direction; and the audit of\narXiv:2603.11066 shows three independently built frameworks\ntranslating term-for-term into one another and hitting the\n\\emph{same} residual wall --- the language-invariance one expects of a\nfaithful compression, not the framework-relativity one would fear.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{The question, made precise}\n\nCall an \\emph{arithmetic mechanism} any constraint usable in a proof:\nan observable of orbits together with a theorem about it. The\nframework under audit speaks the language of valuation words\n$b_n=\\vt(3x_n+1)$, finite character shadows, $2$-adic alignments\n(clocks), and band counting. The referee's worry: perhaps Collatz\ndynamics supports mechanisms invisible in this language, so that\nnarrowing the surviving profile \\emph{inside} the framework\noverstates progress. Faithfulness splits into three claims, each\naddressable: (a) the coding loses nothing; (b) within its declared\ncategories the language is complete; (c) what lies outside is\nisolated explicitly, not silently compressed away. All verification\ncounts refer to \\texttt{search/faithfulness.py}.\n\n\\section{Losslessness: conjugacy, not projection}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Lossless coding]\\label{thm:conj}\nThe word map $x\\mapsto(b_n(x))_{n\\ge0}$ is a homeomorphic conjugacy\nfrom the accelerated Syracuse system on the odd $2$-adics onto the\nfull shift on $\\{1,2,3,\\dots\\}^{\\mathbb N}$, carrying Haar measure to\nthe Bernoulli measure $\\mathbb P[b=k]=2^{-k}$. A length-$k$ prefix\n$w$ pins exactly the residue class $x\\bmod2^{B_w+1}$ and nothing\nmore. (Verified: all $4845$ realizable length-$4$ words each occupy\nexactly one class, total mass $0.9987\\to1$; letter marginals are\nexactly $2^{-k}$ by residue counting.)\n\\end{theorem}\n\nThis is the Bernstein--Lagarias conjugacy in our coordinates; our\ncylinder lemma is its quantitative form. Consequence: \\emph{no}\nmechanism is lost in passing to the symbolic language --- the\n$2$-adic system and the word system are the same object. The language\nhas exactly one blind spot, and it is not a mechanism but a\n\\emph{subset}: $\\mathbb N\\subset\\Ztwo$ (dense, measure zero,\nnon-invariant). The framework does not pretend to express it\nsymbolically; it imports it through four explicit interfaces, each an\nexact theorem: the ghost clocks (positivity caps\n$a\\le\\log_2(|2^K-3^\\ell|x+C)$), without-replacement counting (an\nacyclic orbit visits each integer once), the drift identity (exact,\nwith error $\\sum\\log_2(1+\\tfrac1{3x_n})$ explicitly bounded), and the\nBaker/$S$-unit inputs. Any mechanism the language misses must live in\nthis declared residual --- which is precisely the part the program\ntreats as open.\n\n\\section{Completeness within the finite-modulus category}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[$k$-point shadow completeness]\\label{thm:complete}\nFor any $Q$ coprime to $6$ and any $k$: along any orbit,\n$x_{n+i}\\bmod Q=(3^ix_n+A_i(w))\\,2^{-B_i(w)}\\bmod Q$ for\n$i\\le k$, so \\emph{every} $Q$-periodic observable of a $k$-step\nwindow factors exactly through $(x_n\\bmod Q,\\ b_n,\\dots,b_{n+k-1})$;\nand for every multiplicative character,\n$\\chi(x_{n+1})\\chi(2)^{b_n}=\\chi(3x_n+1)$ exactly --- the keystone\nidentity. (Verified: $2000$ random windows, $Q\\in\\{5,7,11,13,25,35\\}$.)\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[CRT orthogonality]\\label{thm:crt}\nConditional on any word cylinder (an arithmetic progression modulo\n$2^{B+1}$), the residues modulo any odd $m$ are \\emph{exactly}\nequidistributed. Hence the word reads only the $2$-adic coordinate of\n$x$; every other finite place evolves as an explicit skew product\ndriven by the word and carries no information about future letters\nbeyond it. (Verified: $40$ random depth-$18$ cylinders, exact\nuniformity mod $3,5,7$.)\n\\end{theorem}\n\nTogether: \\emph{within the category of finite-modulus observables of\nbounded windows --- the natural home of ``congruence mechanisms'' ---\nthe shadow language is complete, provably and exactly.} A congruence\nmechanism unavailable in the language does not exist.\n\n\\section{The hidden-channel test}\n\nMechanisms outside the congruence category would have to use the\nmultiplicative or global structure of orbit values (factorization,\nprimality, smoothness). \\cref{thm:crt} does not force these to be\nneutral, so we test: among the $2800$ odd $n_0<2^{22}$ surviving\n$23$ letters in $\\{1,2\\}$, against size-matched random odd controls:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{lcccc}\n\\toprule\n & \\text{mean }\\omega(n) & \\mathbb P[\\text{squarefree}] &\n \\mathbb P[3\\mid n] & \\mathbb P[\\text{prime}]\\\\\n\\midrule\n\\text{survivors} & 2.480 & 0.806 & 0.334 & 0.144\\\\\n\\text{controls} & 2.478 & 0.815 & 0.319 & 0.144\\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n(the squarefree density of \\emph{odd} integers is $8/\\pi^2=0.811$;\nboth populations sit on it). Null within sampling error: no\nmultiplicative channel into survival is detected. A deviation here\nwould have been a genuine mechanism outside the language; finding\nnone is the falsifiable content of faithfulness, and the test is\ncheap to repeat at larger depth.\n\nWe record one instructive artifact: ensemble letter autocorrelation\nmeasured naively on $2^{42}$-sized seeds gave $+0.021$, an apparent\nviolation of the Bernoulli prediction --- caused entirely by\nabsorption into the trivial cycle (the constant $b=2$ tail). Measured\non pre-absorption windows it is $-0.003\\pm0.003$. The framework\npredicted both numbers; apparent unfaithfulness was, on inspection,\nthe $+1$ ghost.\n\n\\section{The direction of flow}\n\nThe concern that the program only narrows a surviving profile ---\nreversing Tao's all-integers flow --- describes its\n\\emph{presentation}, not its theorems. The load-bearing results are\nuniversal statements over all integers or all acyclic orbits, in\nexactly Tao's direction:\n\\begin{center}\n\\begin{tabular}{ll}\n\\toprule\n$\\forall$-statement & form\\\\\n\\midrule\nnarrow-band dichotomy & all orbits, dwell $\\le CY^{\\theta(D)}$\\\\\nlogarithmic dwell at ratio $\\le2$ & all acyclic orbits\\\\\nescape rate $O(X\\log X)$ & all divergent orbits\\\\\nupcrossing bound $2^{k-3}$ & all divergent orbits\\\\\ntwo-clock identities, parse & all odd integers, exact\\\\\nuniversal ghost clock, supply & all signatures, all orbits\\\\\nexact counts $N_D(p)$, $(3/4)^D$ law & all words/classes\\\\\nentropy deficit $\\theta_{12}<0.9791$ & all bands, all widths\\\\\nHaar i.i.d.\\ round laws & all residue classes\\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{center}\nThe ``surviving profile'' is the \\emph{complement} of these universal\nconstraints, stated for orientation. Compressing the complement is\nhow universal theorems report progress.\n\n\\section{Language-invariance of the residual}\n\nFinally, the strongest available evidence that the compression is\ncanonical rather than self-serving: independent frameworks built in\ndifferent languages translate into ours term by term. In the audit of\narXiv:2603.11066: their burst--gap calculus \\emph{is} the two-clock\nparse (their $k=\\vt(n+1)$ is our depth $g$; their Persistent Exit\nLemma is our parity handoff at $h=3$, verified $4000/4000$); their\nmean-gap threshold $1.71$ is our $1/\\log_2(3/2)$; their two open\nhypotheses are our two calibration channels; their CIC is the\nparity-$\\equiv1$ extreme of our calibration conjecture; their\nphantom-cycle census is our ghost catalogue with the same roots\n$C_\\sigma/(2^K-3^\\ell)$. Tao's framework (Syracuse random variables,\n$3$-adic drivers, logarithmic density) likewise meets the same\nfinal gap --- almost-all versus all, distributional versus pointwise,\nannealed versus quenched. Three languages, one wall: the obstruction\nis a property of the dynamics, not of any framework. Were the\nfinite-shadow language an unfaithful narrowing, its wall would be an\nartifact located elsewhere than the others'; instead all three walls\ncoincide under explicit dictionaries.\n\nWe also record, for honesty, where the framework's \\emph{stochastic\nheuristics} (as opposed to its language) are known to deviate from\nexact dynamics: the defect-cocycle C-suite measured exact-vs-annealed\ngaps (operator gaps, excursion-length-dependent shadow rates). None\nof the unconditional theorems above rely on annealed models; the\nmeasured gaps are themselves expressed --- and were found ---\n\\emph{inside} the language.\n\n\\section*{Verdict}\n\nFaithful compression $=$ lossless coding $+$ provable completeness on\nthe declared categories $+$ explicitly isolated residual. All three\nhold: the conjugacy (\\cref{thm:conj}), the finite-modulus\ncompleteness theorems (\\cref{thm:complete,thm:crt}, with null\nhidden-channel tests), and the residual --- $\\mathbb N$-positivity,\nthe ghost gap --- which is not compressed away but stated as the open\ncore, where every known framework independently arrives. What would\nfalsify faithfulness is specific and testable: a statistic outside\nthe language that predicts survival beyond its CRT projection. We\nlooked; there is none so far, and the test suite ships with the\nprogram.\n\n\\begin{thebibliography}{9}\n\\bibitem{lagarias} J.~C.~Lagarias, \\emph{The $3x+1$ problem and its\ngeneralizations}, and D.~Bernstein, \\emph{A non-iterative\n$2$-adic statement of the $3N+1$ conjecture} (conjugacy).\n\\bibitem{tao} T.~Tao, \\emph{Almost all orbits of the Collatz map\nattain almost bounded values}, Forum Math.\\ Pi (2022).\n\\bibitem{chang} E.~Y.~Chang, arXiv:2603.11066v6 (2026), audited in\nthe ghost-clock companion note.\n\\bibitem{fss} J.~A.~Janik, \\emph{Finite Spectral Shadows for the\nCollatz Valuation Cocycle} (2026), and companion notes (two clocks;\nuniversal ghost clock; narrow-band; CIC round chain).\n\\end{thebibliography}\n\n\\end{document}\n","file_path":"/home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier/notes/faithfulness.tex"}